# Rank 1838 / CVE-2018-20552 / Bug #520 (recorded language c; the axis is
# CWE-20 input validation of a capture-file length, manifesting as CWE-125/
# CWE-787 downstream). appneta/tcpreplay funnels every packet it reads
# through two validating wrappers in src/common/utils.c,
# _our_safe_pcap_next() and _our_safe_pcap_next_ex(), which call libpcap's
# pcap_next()/pcap_next_ex() and then check the struct pcap_pkthdr those
# calls fill. libpcap validates nothing: for a savefile, caplen and len are
# whatever the file claims. At the parent (2595c903^) the wrappers rejected
# only len > MAXPACKET and len < caplen, so a packet with len == 0 (and
# caplen == 0) passed both guards, and every consumer downstream reads the
# returned buffer at fixed offsets -- pktdata[0], pktdata[3], pktdata[4] in
# src/common/flows.c and src/common/get.c, &pktdata[ETHER_ADDR_LEN] in
# src/bridge.c, packet + SIZE_ETHERNET in src/tcpliveplay.c -- which on a
# zero-length capture is an immediate heap out-of-bounds read. The fixed revision
# 2595c903 prepends !pkthdr->len (and !(*pkthdr)->len) to the second guard
# in both wrappers and touches nothing else: the consumers are unchanged
# across the revision pair.
#
# What fires without this change: nothing on either wrapper. The scan of the
# parent reports findings elsewhere in utils.c (three RawMemoryCopySize rows
# on other functions' memcpy sizes) and none at lines 122-185, and no
# binding anywhere labels a pcap symbol -- the generated libpcap package
# file binds only recv/send/connect/random behind dependency(), which is
# inert for C because the C frontend emits no code.Import (measured at an
# earlier rank on mongoose).
#
# The detection is deliberately not a taint route, because no taint route
# can discriminate this fix, and that is measured rather than assumed. With
# a probe binding labelling pcap_next's return code.NetworkData, the
# consumer shape (caller assigns the wrapper's result and indexes it) fires
# VYQL-MEM-005 with byte-identical fingerprints at the parent and at the
# fix -- a guard added inside the callee clears nothing caller-side. On the
# real tree that route dead-ends even earlier: every consumer reaches the
# wrappers through the safe_pcap_next/safe_pcap_next_ex macros, which the C
# frontend does not expand, so the call sites do not resolve (the macro
# family on file; the same wrapper-and-caller pair gives the
# finding when spelled as a direct call and nothing through the macro). The
# header's own length fields never become tainted at all: pcap_next is not
# in the hardcoded out-parameter reader table, so pkthdr->len stays clean
# (the out-param reader family, likewise on file). What discriminates is
# the wrapper's own guard set, read by shape.
#
# The binding states the wrapper contract from libpcap's documentation: the
# lengths a pcap reader hands out are the capture source's own claims, and
# a wrapper that compares them only against a maximum, or against each
# other, has not excluded zero. Nothing from the fixing commit is named --
# pcap_next/pcap_next_ex are the library's reader API, and the zero
# exclusion is recognised by shape (`!hdr->len`, a deref spelling, or a
# comparison against a zero/one literal), so the guard's variable names do
# not matter and a correctly-fixed wrapper spelled `if (hdr->len == 0)`,
# `len < 1` or `caplen > 0` suppresses exactly like the shipped `!len ||`.
# Residual, stated rather than hidden: a zero test standing alone as
# `if (!hdr->len)` -- no disjunction, no literal -- emits no binary shape
# token at all and is not recognised, so that one fix spelling still
# reports; the decompression sibling (VYQL-MEM-056) carries the same
# residual for `!size` spellings, and the needle philosophy here mirrors
# its shipped list.
#
# Reuse is checked before minting. DecompressionOutputSizeMissingLowerBound
# is the closest judgement -- a peer-controlled length compared against a
# maximum with no comparison against zero -- but its reviewCondition names
# a decompressor sizing an output buffer from the advertised size, with a
# CWE-191/1284 axis; this weakness is a validation gate in front of
# consumer reads, CWE-20/125/787, and widening the shipped concept would
# rewrite VYQL-MEM-056's meaning and the spec that pins it. The remaining
# candidates are per-incident shapes (ZeroLengthRadiusAttributeValueParse,
# DhcpOptionLengthUncheckedRead) or different axes
# (OffsetLengthBoundsOverflow, UncheckedEncodedLengthArithmetic), and
# core.MemoryBoundsCheckIssue has no consuming rule. So the class gets its
# second member, named for the class rather than the incident: any pcap
# reader whose length validation omits the zero bound.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off): the parent
# tree reports 2 (utils.c:125 and :150, the two wrappers) over three runs
# and the fixed tree 0 over three runs; the tree total moves 1156 -> 1158 and
# back. The reachable set outside this repo is enumerable -- every
# pcap_next/pcap_next_ex call site across the clones under /tmp/cve-work/
# is eight files (ntopng PcapInterface.cpp, resiprocate TestRtp.cxx, samba
# ctdb/system_socket.c and examples/pcap2nbench/main.cpp, suricata
# source-pcap-file-helper.c and fuzz_sigpcap.c, tcpdump addrtoname.c and
# ether_ntohost.c); scanning each gives 0, and the suricata src subtree
# scanned whole gives 0. tcpdump's pcap_next_etherent is a distinct exact
# token and does not match; ntopng's `hdr->caplen > 0` is a zero exclusion
# and suppresses; samba's unvalidated readers have no length comparison at
# all and the validating-wrapper anchor declines them.
#
# The cases: (a) and (b) are the two wrappers as the parent had them, the
# deref spelling pinned by (b); (c) is the fixed revision's own form; (d) is the _ex
# fix; (e) and (f) prove the negation is not keyed on the fixed revision's `!`
# spelling -- an equality against zero and a positive caplen bound both
# suppress; (g) is a reader that validates nothing, which the anchor
# declines (no validation is a different finding, not an incomplete one);
# (h) and (i) pin the C++ spelling of the same header.

test "rank1838: safe_pcap_next checks the packet length against caplen and a maximum but never against zero"
  lang c
  file src/common/utils.c
  expect VYQL-MEM-067
  code
  ```
  #include <pcap.h>
  #include <stdio.h>
  #include <stdlib.h>

  #define MAXPACKET 65535

  u_char *_our_safe_pcap_next(pcap_t *pcap, struct pcap_pkthdr *pkthdr,
          const char *funcname, const int line, const char *file)
  {
      u_char *pktdata = (u_char *)pcap_next(pcap, pkthdr);

      if (pktdata) {
          if (pkthdr->len > MAXPACKET) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: %u is greater than maximum %u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, pkthdr->len, MAXPACKET);
              exit(-1);
          }

          if (pkthdr->len < pkthdr->caplen) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: packet length %u is less than capture length %u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, pkthdr->len, pkthdr->caplen);
              exit(-1);
          }
      }

      return pktdata;
  }
  ```

test "rank1838: safe_pcap_next_ex checks the dereferenced header the same incomplete way"
  lang c
  file src/common/utils_ex.c
  expect VYQL-MEM-067
  code
  ```
  #include <pcap.h>
  #include <stdio.h>
  #include <stdlib.h>

  #define MAXPACKET 65535

  int _our_safe_pcap_next_ex(pcap_t *pcap, struct pcap_pkthdr **pkthdr,
          const u_char **pktdata, const char *funcname,
          const int line, const char *file)
  {
      int res = pcap_next_ex(pcap, pkthdr, pktdata);

      if (*pktdata && *pkthdr) {
          if ((*pkthdr)->len > MAXPACKET) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next_ex ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: %u is greater than maximum %u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, (*pkthdr)->len, MAXPACKET);
              exit(-1);
          }

          if ((*pkthdr)->len < (*pkthdr)->caplen) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next_ex ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: packet length %u is less than capture length %u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, (*pkthdr)->len, (*pkthdr)->caplen);
              exit(-1);
          }
      }

      return res;
  }
  ```

test "rank1838: the fixed revision rejects a zero length in the disjunction"
  lang c
  file src/common/utils.c
  reject VYQL-MEM-067
  code
  ```
  #include <pcap.h>
  #include <stdio.h>
  #include <stdlib.h>

  #define MAXPACKET 65535

  u_char *_our_safe_pcap_next(pcap_t *pcap, struct pcap_pkthdr *pkthdr,
          const char *funcname, const int line, const char *file)
  {
      u_char *pktdata = (u_char *)pcap_next(pcap, pkthdr);

      if (pktdata) {
          if (pkthdr->len > MAXPACKET) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: %u is greater than maximum %u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, pkthdr->len, MAXPACKET);
              exit(-1);
          }

          if (!pkthdr->len || pkthdr->len < pkthdr->caplen) {
              fprintf(stderr, "safe_pcap_next ERROR: Invalid packet length in %s:%s() line %d: packet length=%u capture length=%u\n",
                      file, funcname, line, pkthdr->len, pkthdr->caplen);
              exit(-1);
          }
      }

      return pktdata;
  }
  ```

